  abstract: "Constitutive Coordination develops the Constitutive position as a third diagnostic vertex alongside the Augustinian and Pelagian positions. It argues that AI-mediated coordination exposes limits in the assumption that capacities are located somewhere, either supplied from outside or released from within. Some capacities are constituted through the coupling itself, and require a vocabulary that can diagnose them without misattributing them to either side alone."
